GoogleService-Info.plist

# Generated by `flutterfire configure`. Ignored because this repository is
# public: the file carries the Firebase API key and project identifiers, and
# Flutter's own docs say not to commit it when the app calls Gemini from the
# client, since anyone could reuse the config against the AI endpoint and burn
# the quota. App Check makes that much harder, but harder is not impossible and
# ignoring the file costs nothing. Same treatment as key.properties: absent on
# a fresh clone, regenerated by `flutterfire configure`.
lib/firebase_options.dart

# Also written by `flutterfire configure`. No key in it — just the project and
# app ids — and those are already discoverable from any shipped APK, so this is
# caution rather than necessity. Ignored to keep the Firebase surface uniformly
# absent from a public repo; `flutterfire configure` regenerates it on demand.
# Note this departs from FlutterFire's own convention, which is to commit it.
firebase.json

